   "transcript": "[Speaker] Example 0 Sure, buddy. Here, have a Dr Pepper.\n[Speaker] Question 1 Well… it’s the oldest major manufacturer of soft drink concentrates and syrups in the United States. It’s a unique soft drink due to its twenty-three flavours and secret recipe. It was first created, manufactured and sold in 1885 in the Central Texas town of Waco at Morrison’s Old Corner Drug Store, one whole year before Coca Cola was invented by Dr John Pemberton in Atlanta.\n[Speaker] Question 2 Dr Pepper was invented by a young pharmacist called Charles Alderton who worked at Morrison’s store in downtown Wako. Although he spent most of his day mixing medicines for the local Texans, he also served carbonated drinks at the soda fountain in the store, because he liked the smell of the fruits and syrups that mixed together in the air. In fact, he liked them so much that he decided to create a drink that tasted just the same as that smell.\n[Speaker] Question 3 Well, after numerous tests and tasting sessions with the store’s owner, Alderton started to serve the drink to the fountain customers.\n[Speaker] Question 4 Well now, it was affectionately known as a ‘Wako’ until Mr Morrison, the store owner, officially named it Dr Pepper after a Dr Charles Pepper who was a Virginia doctor and the father of a girl that Morrison was once in love with. Dr Pepper gained such widespread popularity that Morrison and Alderton could not produce enough of the product to supply the demand.\n[Speaker] Question 5 Alderton suggested that a young beverage chemist, Robert Lazenby, take over the development of the drink with Morrison and he went back to his pharmacy work. In 1904, Dr Pepper was introduced to the 20 million people who visited the World’s Fair Exhibition in St. Louis and it was an instant success. Interestingly enough, it wasn’t the only major product to be introduced at that fair. Hamburgers, hot dogs and ice cream cones were served in huge numbers. Morrison and Lazenby were very pleased with the success of Dr Pepper and they formed a new company, the Artesian Mfg and Bottling Company which later became the Dr Pepper Company.\n[Speaker] Question 6 People just liked the taste and the company continued to grow. In 1923 it was moved to Dallas where it went on to become one of America’s biggest refreshments. Today it is one of the world’s favourite drinks.\n[Speaker] Question 7 Oh yes, the best and it shows how grateful it is by being committed to diversity and sponsoring many multicultural programs.",
